{
  "title": "Pangea™ 3.5 Distal Medial Femur Plate",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/implants/423192/pangea-tm--35-distal-medial-femur-plate",
  "subtitle": "Distal Femur Fractures Updated: Dec 5 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Related Implants",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea™ series contains 3 distal femur plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Distal Lateral Femur**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**3.5 Distal Medial Femur (this topic)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**5.0 Distal Medial Femur**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Variable Angle Locking Screw Holes**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Pangea’s variable angle locking technology uses a CoCr locking screw, which is harder than the Ti6Al4V ELI plate, allowing for the screwhead’s threads to form a definitive plate-screw interface in the plate's locking hole by engaging the softer, Ti6Al4V material.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423192/images/4baa2c48-2fd4-485d-930f-b42c96744f2f_image.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "This technology allows the user to aim and lock the screw into the plate within a true 30° cone of the predetermined hole trajectory. The variable angle drill guide provided with the system offers guidance with respect to the limit of the 30° cone. The locking mechanism remains functional for up to three attempts at locking screw insertion.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Circular holes that accommodate screws are universal; accepting non-locking and locking screws within a 30° cone.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**2.0mm K-Wire Holes**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "To provide temporary fixation.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423192/images/4baa2c48-2fd4-485d-930f-b42c96744f2f_image.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Metaphyseal Screw Holes**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423192/images/4baa2c48-2fd4-485d-930f-b42c96744f2f_image.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "10 universal holes allowing for fracture fixation.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Placement",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Once reduction is achieved, the plate is placed on the anteromedial surface of the distal femur",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423192/images/a444804e-d9f9-4653-b62f-058e2d9bc5fa_plate_position.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Plates have been designed using SOMA software. In most cases, the precontoured plate will fit without the need for additional adjustments.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Plate is in the proper position when the distal end of the plate is adjacent to the medial articular margin of the trochlea and anterior to the medial epicondyle.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Plate placement designed to reduce the potential for interference with the medial collateral ligament.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The surgeon must be familiar with the vascular anatomy of the thigh to ensure that proximal screw insertion will not put vascular structures at risk.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fit",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Designed with the use of SOMA: Stryker Orthopedics Modeling and Analytics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "SOMA includes a database with CT scans from hospitals across the world and state of the art algorithms to mine the data for shape variability, bone density, and implant fit.1",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Can be used for Periprosthetic fractures around a femoral component, and extra-articular fractures where a nail cannot be used",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "3.5mm Distal Medial Femur plate may be used for isolated medial condylar fractures or as a supplement to lateral plate fixation when dual plate fixation is desired.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea Femur Plating System is indicated for the internal fixation and stabilization of femur bone fractures and osteotomies in normal and osteopenic bone, including:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Diaphyseal, metaphyseal, epiphyseal, extra- and intra-articular fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Non-unions, malunions, and deformities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Periprosthetic fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Approaches",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Surgeons may use a standard medial, medial parapatellar, or medial subvastus approach to the distal medial femur",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technical specifications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Standard plate lengths: 96mm- 152mm (2 to 6 holes)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Thickness: 4.0mm",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Left and right anatomic plate options",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Drill bits: 2.5mm drill bit (542020)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
